{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.3a79fafbe4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-637","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Rahman is a Vietnamese architect.</li><li>In 1974, Rahman designed the Fairhaven Community Center.</li><li>The Fairhaven Community Center is lit almost entirely by skylights during the day.</li><li>The Fairhaven Community Center won a national design award.</li><li>Rahman trained at a design school in Copenhagen.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe a distinctive feature of the Fairhaven Community Center.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Fairhaven Community Center, designed by Rahman, is lit almost entirely by skylights during the day.","The Fairhaven Community Center won a national design award.","The Fairhaven Community Center was designed in 1974.","Amara Rahman trained at a design school in Copenhagen."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It states what makes the work distinctive. The other choices give a date, an achievement, or background about the creator."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.653a75ef21","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-644","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Solberg is a Norwegian architect.</li><li>In 1988, Solberg designed the Copper Falls Concert Hall.</li><li>The Copper Falls Concert Hall uses timber from sustainably managed forests.</li><li>The Copper Falls Concert Hall was named the region's best new public building.</li><li>Solberg trained at a design school in Copenhagen.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize the success of the Copper Falls Concert Hall.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Zara Solberg trained at a design school in Copenhagen.","The Copper Falls Concert Hall, designed by Solberg, uses timber from sustainably managed forests.","The Copper Falls Concert Hall was named the region's best new public building.","The Copper Falls Concert Hall was designed in 1988."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It reports what the work achieved. The other choices describe its features, its date, or the creator's background."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.48f6a66a13","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-14","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Novak is a psychologist.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.</li><li>Novak had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.</li><li>Novak found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.</li><li>Novak concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Novak found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.","To investigate the question, Novak had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.","Novak concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.","Psychologist Elias Novak set out to learn whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.7baed5419f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-17","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Nakamura is a psychologist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.</li><li>Nakamura had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.</li><li>Nakamura found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nakamura found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.","Psychologist Zara Nakamura set out to learn whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.","Nakamura concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.","To investigate the question, Nakamura had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.d833c80361","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-23","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Nakamura is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Nakamura grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Nakamura found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nakamura concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","Nakamura found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.","To investigate the question, Nakamura grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.","Agricultural scientist Nadia Nakamura set out to learn whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.f7bc896c60","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-56","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Beatriz Haddad is a zoologist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Haddad gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Haddad found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Zoologist Beatriz Haddad set out to learn whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.","To investigate the question, Haddad gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.","Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","Haddad found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.9ecf068152","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-73","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Vance is an economist.</li><li>Vance wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Vance tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Vance found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Vance concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Vance tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.","Vance found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.","Economist Dmitri Vance set out to learn whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.","Vance concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.b58919acbf","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-102","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Mbeki is a chemist.</li><li>Mbeki wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Mbeki placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Mbeki found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Mbeki concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mbeki found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Mbeki concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.","Chemist Nadia Mbeki set out to learn whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.","To investigate the question, Mbeki placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.bc883c65b2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-143","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Castellano is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Castellano scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Castellano found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Castellano concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Castellano found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.","To investigate the question, Castellano scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.","Castellano concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.","Neuroscientist Tomás Castellano set out to learn whether learning to juggle changes brain structure."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.6a30a34ede","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-148","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kwame Ferreira is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Ferreira fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Ferreira found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Ferreira fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.","Marine ecologist Kwame Ferreira set out to learn whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.","Ferreira found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.","Ferreira concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.54341b439e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-150","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Varga is a climate scientist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Varga compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Varga found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Varga concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Varga compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.","Varga found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","Varga concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","Climate scientist Chen Varga set out to learn whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.8cf53f70b8","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-177","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Vance is a music researcher.</li><li>Vance wanted to find out whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.</li><li>Vance tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.</li><li>Vance found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.</li><li>Vance concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Vance concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.","To investigate the question, Vance tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.","Vance found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.","Music researcher Zara Vance set out to learn whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."}
